# video.limits: the clips whose dropped frames judge.py video prints and
# does not judge on Rach2, one a line by the name of the clip's plays file
# without `.plays`. Firefox's decoder threads make some 4,300 futex calls
# and 7,800 page faults a second, which Rach2 serves one processor at a
# time under its big kernel lock, so Firefox drops more frames than the
# Debian guest under the references' load (tests/graphics/Readme.md,
# Limits). The lines go once futex, page faults and the timer tick no
# longer take that lock.
firefox-h264-720p.mp4
firefox-h264-1080p.mp4
firefox-vp9-720p.webm
firefox-vp9-1080p.webm
firefox-av1-720p.webm
firefox-av1-1080p.webm
